        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic itself is placed well and reuses the right units \u2014 `rejectCityAtCapacity` mirrors the existing `rejectDuplicateTelephone`/`rejectDuplicateHousehold` guards, it correctly reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper rather than duplicating the stream/normalization logic, and the exception + handler pair faithfully follow the established `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` pattern (advice-package exception carrying the offending value, a parallel `@ExceptionHandler` with the same logging/`detailBuild`/`setProperty(\"errors\", ...)` shape). That part is idiomatic.\n\nOne structural inconsistency worth fixing:\n\n- **`CITY_CAPACITY` constant is declared in the wrong place.** The class establishes a clear convention of grouping `private static final` constants at the top of the class (`EMAIL_PATTERN` at line 72, `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` at line 79). The new constant is instead buried at line 419, interleaved among the private helper methods (between `countOwnersInCity` and `rejectDuplicateTelephone`). A maintainer scanning for the class's tunable constants would expect it alongside the others at the top. Move the `CITY_CAPACITY` declaration (with its doc comment) up to the constant block at the top of the class, leaving `rejectCityAtCapacity` where it is."
